Keep a shared source as empty text.
Place "3[a]2[bc]" into source.
Keep a shared cursor as 0.
Keep a shared frames as an empty list of text.
Keep a shared counts as an empty list of whole numbers.
Keep a shared multiplier as 0.
The base is empty text.
Place base into frames.

To gather.
Set multiplier to 0.
For every step from 0 to the last position of source.
The here is cursor.
If here is more than the last position of source, break.
If character here of source is not between "0" and "9", break.
The digit is the digit value of character here of source.
Set multiplier to multiplier times 10 plus digit.
Add 1 to cursor.

To enter.
The fresh is empty text.
Place fresh into frames.
Place multiplier into counts.
Set multiplier to 0.
Add 1 to cursor.

To unwind.
The depth is the number of items in frames.
The part is item (depth minus 1) of frames.
The times is item (depth minus 2) of counts.
Remove the last item from frames.
Remove the last item from counts.
The duplicate is a copy of part.
The parent is item (depth minus 2) of frames.
Add 1 to cursor.
For every step from 1 to times.
Place duplicate into parent.
Set item (depth minus 2) of frames to parent.

To emit.
The depth is the number of items in frames.
The here is cursor.
The piece is the slice of source from here to here plus 1.
The current is item (depth minus 1) of frames.
Place piece into current.
Set item (depth minus 1) of frames to current.
Add 1 to cursor.

Repeat while cursor is at most the last position of source.
The here is cursor.
The symbol is character here of source.
If symbol is between "0" and "9", gather.
If symbol is "[", enter.
If symbol is "]", unwind.
If symbol is not between "0" and "9" and symbol is not "[" and symbol is not "]", emit.

Show item 0 of frames.
